  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "Given that \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are distinct nonzero real numbers such that \\(x + \\dfrac{2}{x} = y + \\dfrac{2}{y},\\) what is \\(xy?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2013-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Multiplying by \\(xy\\) gives \\(x^2 y + 2y = xy^2 + 2x,\\) so \\[ \\begin{gathered} x^2 y - xy^2 - 2x + 2y \\\\ = (x - y)(xy - 2) \\\\ = 0. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nSince \\(x \\ne y,\\) it follows that \\(xy = 2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Multiply both sides by \\(xy\\) to clear the fractions",
        "The result factors as \\((x - y)(xy - 2) = 0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
